    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-09T17:32:29+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-09T17:32:29+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T07:02:29Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T07:02:29Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough and cold front clear to the east of the state state overnight, as a high pressure system briefly establishes in the north on Saturday. Another series of troughs and cold fronts are expected to enter western SA early on Sunday, crossing the state and then clearing in the east by the end of Monday. A ridge of high pressure will then push into western SA on Monday before the associated high moves into waters south on Tuesday. A trough over the WA/NT border will also extend into SA at times from Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <warning-summary type="fire_weather_warning" start-time-local="2026-10-09T04:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-08T17:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">Fire Weather Warning for the North East Pastoral fire weather district for Friday</warning-summary>
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-09T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Patchy raised dust near the eastern border early this evening. High chance of showers near the eastern border, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to southwesterly 35 to 50 km/h tending north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h in the late afternoon then tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 34.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening, possibly severe with damaging winds west of Leigh Creek. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h before dawn then tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 32 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds east of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 40 km/h turning southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
